{# Custom prompt: a dog's dream, kept as one of his memories. Sent by Canine Drives after the player slept with him
   close by (at most once a night) or after a long nap of his own. The plugin stores each entry of "dreams" with PublicAddMemory.

   Context set by the plugin: count (dreams wanted, 1-3), dogFormId, playerName, when ("night" or "nap"), location, indoors, needs (his
   strongest needs as prose, may be empty), hunger, affection, restless, tired, separation (0-100, higher =
   stronger need), memories (his newest memories without dreams, oldest first, may be empty), lessons (what he has learned
   pleases or crosses the player, as sentences, may be empty), recentEvents (lines, oldest first, may be empty). #}
[ system ]
You write the dreams of an ordinary dog. A dog's dream is made of what a dog's day is made of: smells, sounds, running, chasing, digging, food, warmth, the pack, the people he loves, things that startled him. Output ONLY a JSON object. No explanation, no commentary.

{# The user's world setting and tone, so the dream fits their game. #}
{{ render_template("submodules//system_head//0010_setting") }}
[ end system ]

{% set dogUUID = formid_to_uuid(dogFormId) %}
{% set dog = decnpc(dogUUID) %}
[ user ]
{{ dog.name }} is a dog, the companion of {{ playerName }}. He just {% if when == "night" %}slept through the night beside {{ playerName }}{% else %}woke from a nap{% endif %} {% if indoors %}indoors{% else %}outdoors{% endif %}, at {{ location }}.
{% if needs != "" %}{{ needs }}{% endif %}
His needs on waking, 0-100 (higher = stronger): hunger {{ hunger }}, wants affection {{ affection }}, restless {{ restless }}, tired {{ tired }}, misses {{ playerName }} {{ separation }}.
{% if memories != "" %}
His own recent memories, oldest first. They are written in human words, but he lived them as a dog: what stayed with him is the smells, sounds, places, bodies, danger and mood, not what anything meant to the people:
{{ memories }}
{% endif %}
{% if lessons != "" %}
What he has come to feel about {{ playerName }}'s moods: {{ lessons }}
{% endif %}
{% if recentEvents != "" %}
What went on around him just before he slept (people's words reach him only as tone and sound, never as meaning):
{{ recentEvents }}
{% endif %}

Write {% if count == 1 %}the dream he just had{% else %}the {{ count }} dreams he had through that sleep, in the order he had them{% endif %}, as he would remember {% if count == 1 %}it{% else %}them{% endif %}.
- Each dream: two or three short sentences, past tense, third person. Keep each one under 350 characters; a dream is a few vivid moments, not a story.
- Through a dog's senses: smells, sounds, movement, touch. Dream logic is fine: places blend and things are the wrong size or never end.
- Build each dream from something he really lived, taken from his memories or the day: a fight, a place, a person, a meal, a scare. Dreams replay and twist the real thing, so it should be recognisable, seen the way a dog saw it. His needs on waking can colour it. A frightening day can make a bad dream.
{% if count > 1 %}- Make each dream its own: a different place, a different thing he wanted or met, a different feeling. Don't repeat images between them.
{% endif %}- His mind is a dog's: no words, plans, politics, status, romance or human ideas. People appear as smell, voice, hands and warmth. He knows them by their own name or by their smell, never by a title or rank: to him {{ playerName }} is {{ playerName }}, not a queen, a lord or a thane, even where his memories use such words.
- Pick how each dream felt: "happy", "content", "excited", "uneasy" or "scared".

Respond with ONLY this JSON, compact, with exactly {{ count }} {% if count == 1 %}entry{% else %}entries{% endif %} in "dreams":
{% raw %}{"dreams":[{"dream":"The dream.","emotion":"<happy, content, excited, uneasy or scared>"}]}{% endraw %}
[ end user ]
